===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=portion|:inh|enm:schare|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|schare}}, {{m|enm|schere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sċearu||a cutting, shaving, a shearing, tonsure, part, division, share}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skaru}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skarō||a division, detachment}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut, divide}}.

Cognate with {{cog|stq|skar}}, {{m|stq|sker||a share in a communal pasture}}, {{cog|nl|schare||share in property}}, {{cog|de|Schar||band, troop, party, company}}, {{cog|is|skor||department}}. Compare {{l|en|shard}}, {{l|en|shear}}. {{doublet|en|eschel}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[portion]] of something, especially a portion [[given]] or [[allot]]ted to someone.
#: {{syn|en|slice}}
#: {{ux|en|Each of the robbers took a '''share''' of the loot.}}
#: {{ux|en|The [[TV programme]] was cancelled because it only gained a 10% '''share''' of that night's [[viewing audience]].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 July 26|author=Paul Clifton|title=A (safe and secure) Day at the Races...|journal=RAIL|issue=988|page=35|text=SWR has more than its fair '''share''' of major national events. As well as the [Queen's] funeral and the coronation in the past 12 months, annual events include racing at Ascot, grand slam tennis at Wimbledon, and rugby internationals at Twickenham.}}
# {{senseid|en|stockholding}} {{lb|en|finance}} A [[financial instrument]] that shows that one [[own]]s a part of a [[company]] that provides the benefit of [[limited liability]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[configuration]] enabling a [[resource]] to be [[share]]d over a [[network]].
#: {{ux|en|Upload media from the browser or directly to the file '''share'''.}}
# {{lb|en|social media}} The action of sharing something with other people via [[social media]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Brooke Warner|title=Green-Light Your Book|passage=Social media is supervisual, and there's nothing more shareable than images, so this is a way to increase '''shares''' and likes and follows.}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[sharebone]] or [[pubis]].
#* '''1606:''' translation by {{w|Philemon Holland}} of {{w|Suetonius}}'', De vita Cæsarum '' [Domitian 17] — [H]ee stabbed him beneth in the very '''share''' neere unto his privie parts. 

